## Why This Is Asked

Tests the ability to design hierarchical online PCA for nonstationary, multi-region telemetry with strict latency constraints.

## Key Concepts

- **Online/Incremental PCA**: Updates principal components incrementally as new data arrives, avoiding full recomputation
- **Hierarchical Components**: Regional vs. global decomposition captures both local variation and shared patterns
- **Drift Detection in Loadings**: Monitors changes in eigenvectors over time to identify concept drift
- **Region-Global Consistency**: Ensures global components reflect true cross-regional phenomena, not artifacts
- **Latency-Aware Processing**: Complete pipeline must fit within 5-second alert window

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudocode: Update regional/global PCs on new batch
function updateRegion(region, X_batch) {
  // Impute missing values before fitting
  const X_clean = imputeMissing(region, X_batch);

  // Incrementally update regional PCA
  region.pca.partialFit(X_clean);

  // Check for drift in loadings
  region.driftMonitor.check(region.pca.loadings);
}

function updateGlobal(allRegionalPCs) {
  // Aggregate regional scores for global model
  const X_global = stackRegionalScores(allRegionalPCs);
  global.pca.partialFit(X_global);
  global.driftMonitor.check(global.pca.loadings);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you adapt the component counts as data drift occurs?
- How would you validate the drift detection and confirm it is not false alarm?
- How would you handle communication delays between regions?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design an online, drift-aware PCA system that remains interpretable and compliant under strict latency constraints typical of autonomous vehicle systems.

## Key Concepts
- Online incremental PCA (IPCA) with forgetting factors
- Concept drift detection and adaptation strategies
- Dynamic feature addition/removal via partial-fit methods
- Loading stability tracking for interpretability preservation
- Millisecond-latency optimization through parallel computation
- Governance-aligned explainability through loading-to-alert mappings

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo: partial_fit on new data, adjust window, recompute top loadings
function updateIPCA(newData, currentModel, windowSize, forgettingFactor) {
  // Partial fit with forgetting factor
  const updatedModel = partialFit(newData, currentModel, forgettingFactor);
  // Adjust moving window
  const windowedModel = adjustWindow(updatedModel, windowSize);
  // Recpute interpretable loadings
  return computeTopLoadings(windowedModel);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you set drift-detection thresholds to balance automatic fallback versus adaptation?
- What validation approach would you use comparing synthetic drift scenarios against real-world telemetry patterns?
- How do you ensure loading stability while maintaining computational efficiency?

## Why This Is Asked

